WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.300
Thank you so much
for coming on, bud.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.534
-Nice to see you.
Thanks for having me.

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:05.734
-I missed you.
The last couple times we talked

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:07.701
was through Zoom.
-Yeah, which is crazy.

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:08.934
-Yeah, and now we're here.

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:10.100
Thank you for being here
in person.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.834
How are you?
How's the family?

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:13.167
-I'm good.
Everybody's good.

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:14.634
Kids are good.
They're all almost grown.

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:18.434
You know, we're about to have
our own little empty nest.

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:19.901
Yeah.
-You are, really?

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:22.501
-Well, not, yet,
but, like, my youngest is 12.

00:00:22.501 --> 00:00:24.300
-You've got some time.
-It's right around the corner.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.734
[ Laughter ]
It goes by fast.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.434
-That's got years.
You got years yet.

00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:29.300
-She's already
traveling the world

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.901
jumping horses
and doing her thing.

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:34.167
-You sent me a photo here.
Here, look at this.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.934
How gorgeous.
Come on. How cute is that?

00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:37.400
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.167
-Of course, she picked the most
expensive sport possible, but...

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:41.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.033
-Did you try to talk
her out of it or anything?

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:44.334
-No, she loves it.

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:46.300
And she takes so much pride
in the little stuff.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.868
She's at the barn every day
shoveling poop.

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:51.000
-Taking care.
-Yeah, she's up before me.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.467
-Look at this shot.
This is great.

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:54.801
Look at this.
-But do you notice,

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:56.167
she's looking
at the photographer?

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:57.300
She's not looking where
she's supposed to be jumping.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.834
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, she knows.

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:01.801
She's like "Insta, Insta," yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:03.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:05.534
And how are the boys?
-Boys are good.

00:01:05.534 --> 00:01:08.634
I got them playing golf.
-That's amazing.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:11.434
-And now my wife can't tell me
I can't go play.

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:12.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:13.701
I just say
I'm going with the kids.

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:16.767
-Yeah, it's daddy-son time.
It's a boys trip.

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:19.901
-We just went to England and
Ireland and played and hung out.

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:21.334
-That must be amazing.

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:22.767
-No, I didn't give them
any Guinness.

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:24.501
They're 16 and 14.
-I didn't ask that --

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:25.601
-Don't imply
that I gave them beer.

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:27.200
-I didn't ask that question
at all.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.100
[ Laughter ]
-No, 16 and 13, almost 14.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.701
-I'm sure, 16, yeah, yeah.

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:33.434
Are they good at golf?
Are they like their dad?

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:34.734
-They're better than me.

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:36.701
They started young,
so they were smart, you know?

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:38.200
They like --
Well, actually they started --

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.868
they were on punishment,
so they could only play golf,

00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:42.033
which was good.

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:43.801
And then they actually
started to like it.

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:45.434
So now they're continuing
to play.

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:46.968
-Yeah, I think that's the way
to do it.

00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:49.367
Why not? Yeah.
-Put them on lockdown

00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:51.667
and give them a club.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:54.467
-I saw a photo,
you and James Caan together here

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:57.000
at a golf tournament.
He just passed away.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.567
This is you, James Caan,
and Sylvester Stallone

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:01.634
at a charity --
This is at an event.

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.133
-I believe
it was at Jimmy's event.

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:07.434
Yeah, he threw an event
every year at El Cab.

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:09.300
-What was he like?
What was James Caan like?

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.968
-The best.
-Just great.

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:12.167
-The first time
I worked with him, he goes,

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:13.601
"You know I'm a dream
to work with, right?"

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:15.667
And then I literally called him
"The Dream" ever since.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.901
-Is that right? "You know,
I'm a dream to work with."

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.534
-He's amazing.
I got to spend some time

00:02:19.534 --> 00:02:22.300
with him not too long ago,
actually.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.601
We went to go and visit
another friend.

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:25.601
I went to his house, hung out,
and then we realized

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:27.734
we had another friend,
who was a dear friend of ours

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:30.100
who was not well.
So we kind of put Jimmy

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.934
in the car, we went to see him,
and we got to -- yeah.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:34.667
-He's a good guy, right?
-Yeah.

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:36.167
It just puts things
into perspective.

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:38.968
I mean, life goes by so short.
So anybody, you know,

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:41.133
people, friends getting older,
reach out to them.

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:42.734
Tell them you love them.

00:02:42.734 --> 00:02:44.767
Stay as close and connected
as possible.

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:49.667
-We're gonna miss James Caan.
[ Applause ]

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:51.868
I want to talk about
your new movie, "Me Time."

00:02:51.868 --> 00:02:55.300
Because you know, Kevin Hart,
he's a pal of the show,

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.701
and I think you guys
would be great together.

00:02:56.701 --> 00:02:58.067
Is this the first time
you guys worked together?

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:00.634
-It is.
You know, he came --

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:02.601
We met long ago, and he was
like, "I want to work with you.

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:04.667
I want to work with you."
So I like, "Cool. I can't wait."

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:06.567
And then I'd, like, send him
all these different ideas.

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:08.467
He passed on everything
I sent him.

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:10.267
[ Laughter ]
And then all of a sudden,

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:12.801
he sends me a movie
where I'm supporting him.

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:15.267
And then he's got me
ass naked -- excuse my language.

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:17.200
He's got me in Daisy Dukes
on a boat.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.834
I'm like,
is this supposed to be funny,

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:21.400
or is it just making fun of me?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.968
-I think the first scene, you
were naked in the first scene.

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:25.434
-Yeah.
In the very first scene,

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:27.534
in front of like, you know,
a crew of 200 people,

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:29.767
another hundred extras.

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:32.167
But I had sneakers on.
-That counts.

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:35.934
-I had some Travis Scott's on.
-That counts as something, yeah.

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:37.834
And I heard that you invited him

00:03:37.834 --> 00:03:39.734
to work out with you,
and he refused, Kevin.

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:41.667
-Oh, he never showed up.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:44.133
He's so busy,
he barely showed up to work.

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:46.267
I mean, I was just looking
at our text chain earlier.

00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:47.634
And it's like,
"I'm on my way, buddy.

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.667
I'll be right there.
Running five behind.

00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:51.501
I'm five minutes behind."
Always -- yeah.

00:03:51.501 --> 00:03:53.801
-He's doing something.
-Yeah, which is amazing.

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:56.200
I mean, he really, kind of --
We started joking about it,

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.801
about all the different things
that we do

00:03:57.801 --> 00:03:59.868
outside of our primary business.

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:01.400
-Kevin Hart's
the busiest man on Earth.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:04.033
-Yeah, but you know what?
what I loved about him

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:06.100
and I love about you,
and I love about Will Ferrell,

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.734
is that guys --
just genuinely nice guys

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:10.033
who just genuinely
like to make people laugh.

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:11.234
-Aw, yeah.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:04:11.234 --> 00:04:12.767
And when you get into
the snapping and going

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:15.334
back and forth with Kevin,
he'll start it.

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:16.801
He'll say something
to insult you.

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:19.834
But then he'll say something
after when you come back at him

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:22.400
to make you feel bad.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.434
-He'll say something real nice.
-He's really slick.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:29.133
-He is a pro.
-He's finessed it.

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:31.767
-Can you tell me what the
movie's about and who you play?

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:34.367
-I play a guy named Huck Dembo,
who's his best friend

00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:35.868
who's never quite grown up.

00:04:35.868 --> 00:04:39.767
Kev plays the stay-at-home dad
whose wife is finally like,

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:41.534
she's going on a job,
she's taking the kids,

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:43.434
so she's kind of encouraged him
to go and have fun.

00:04:43.434 --> 00:04:45.234
-Yeah.
-And I've never grown up.

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:46.701
I'm hanging around with,
basically,

00:04:46.701 --> 00:04:50.434
teenagers or kids half my age,
and I screw up his whole life.

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:52.767
Everything that he has
that's safe and comfortable

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:55.734
gets destroyed by my craziness.

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:57.133
-He's just trying
to get a little me time.

00:04:57.133 --> 00:04:58.801
-Yes.
-And you destroy his life.

00:04:58.801 --> 00:05:02.133
-Yes.
And it's quite fun and funny.

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:04.300
Because John Hamburg,
who's fantastic --

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.501
he wrote and directed it --
he's just done this great job

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:08.100
of really kind of
making it entertaining

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.534
for both kids and adults.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:11.434
Like there's lots of great
adult humor in there,

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:12.868
but kids don't quite get it.

00:05:12.868 --> 00:05:14.501
And then there's lots of great
stuff for the kids, as well.

00:05:14.501 --> 00:05:15.767
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:15.767 --> 00:05:17.801
Here's Mark Wahlberg
and Kevin Hart in "Me Time."

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:19.100
Take a look at this.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.400
-Wake up!
-Don't flick him!

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.801
You have to gently grasp.

00:05:22.801 --> 00:05:28.033
Cover his mouth and blow slow,
steady breaths into his nostril.

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:30.000
[ Tires screech ]

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.200
-We're here, fools.
-Wait! Wait!

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:33.834
Stop, stop!
I said, "Don't."

00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:35.667
-I got it.
-Go on.

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:37.200
Car.
Car, car.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.367
-Slow down!
-Hey!

00:05:39.367 --> 00:05:43.400
[ Horn honks ]

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.734
-Hey, you got it from here?
-I got it.

00:05:45.734 --> 00:05:47.200
[ Buzzer ]
[ Horn honking ]

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:52.234
-Let's go, you idiot!

00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:53.467
-Hold on, hold on.
Wait.

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:54.834
Wait, wait, wait!
-What?!

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:57.300
[ Door opens, bell chimes ]
-God damn it.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:59.667
Did you do this?

00:05:59.667 --> 00:06:00.667
-No!

00:06:00.667 --> 00:06:01.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:01.834 --> 00:06:04.367
-Busted.
Busted.

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:05.667
Mark Wahlberg, everybody.

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:09.100
"Me Time" premieres on Netflix
August 26th.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.000
Mark and I are playing a fun
game when we come back.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.634
Stick around, everybody.

